Exact source: overeem11/RAINLINK commit
ce355d68dcb59ec17f75d05babc4a6f6d2ee90f0, archived privately with source,
paper, original runtime and qualification evidence. Local Python mathematics
replaces the domain-library dependencies; no RAINLINK, gstat, sf or s2 package
is called by the cleaned runtime.

Qualifications: two header=TRUE coefficient-file reads in the private original
driver preserve all numeric coefficients. The main binding consistently selects
the paper's full wet/dry option; the sequential demonstration's final overwritten
no-wet/dry result is preserved as a separate actual original comparison.

The actual T-Mobile Netherlands/Nokia sample data are author-supplied public
research observations. The paper expressly describes the RAINLINK link dataset
as freely available for all parties. No independent additional data license
grant was identified; the GPL declaration on software is not asserted to grant
ownership or unrestricted redistribution rights in third-party measurements.
Public redistribution of those measurements remains unresolved; this package is
maintainer-only local research staging. No contact with data owners was made.

The reconstructed field is a conditional method estimate, not rainfall truth.
Spatial midpoint, stationary covariance and effective wet-antenna assumptions
remain scientific limitations. The dataset is measured; no new target or noise
observations were manufactured for the binding.
